{"name":"Elusive Dream","hex":"#cdbfc6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elusive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Evading capture, comprehension or remembrance.","Difficult to make precise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elusive"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elusive","blocks":[{"text":"\"Elusive\" was the first single for British singer-songwriter Scott Matthews and was released on 18 September 2006. The single received much airplay from BBC Radio DJs Jo Whiley, Dermot O'Leary and Zane Lowe between 7 and 10 August. Lowe also played \"Elusive\" once each night as his chosen Single of the Week. Matthews also visited the station to perform \"Elusive\" and other songs from the album in May and August 2006. In May 2007, he won the Ivor Novello Award for \"Best Song Musically and Lyrically\" which saw \"Elusive\" beat strong competition from the likes of the Arctic Monkeys."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elusive"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Raja_Ravi_Varma%2C_Usha%27s_Dream_%28oleographic_print